# Copy to .env for local `npm run dev`. Never commit .env (it is gitignored).
#
# THIS FILE IS BUILD-TIME, .dev.vars.example IS RUNTIME, and the split is not cosmetic.
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the CLIENT bundle when `react-router build` runs, so
# these have to be present at BUILD time (a GitHub repo variable, read by CI's deploy job,
# or this file locally). Server secrets live in .dev.vars locally and in
# `wrangler secret` in production, and are never inlined into a browser bundle.

# Google Maps JavaScript API, used by app/components/data/DataMap.client.tsx.
#
# A browser Maps key is PUBLIC by construction: it ships inside the client bundle and anyone
# can read it. That is the normal shape for this API, and the control that matters is not
# secrecy but an HTTP-REFERRER RESTRICTION set on the key in the Google Cloud console, plus a
# billing quota. An unrestricted key is a key anyone can spend.
#
# Without this set the map does not render and the page falls back to its data table, which is
# the accessible equivalent and carries the same numbers.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=

# Advanced Markers render ONLY on a map that has a Map ID, so this is required rather than
# decorative. Leave it empty to use Google's DEMO_MAP_ID, which is fine for development and
# should be a real Map ID (Google Cloud console, Map Management) before launch.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
